  <wpt lat="52.344335" lon="-67.378378"><name>Dirt Road Section Starts (Fire Lake Unpaved QC-389)</name><desc>[Day 3] (hazard) ⚠️ Paved highway ends and unpaved gravel road section begins near Fire Lake Mine. Reduce speed to 70–80 km/h and stand on pegs over washboard.</desc><type>hazard</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.771881" lon="-67.322654"><name>Dirt Road Stops Here — Pavement Begins (Mont-Wright)</name><desc>[Day 3] (hazard) ✅ Northern end of the Fire Lake–Mont-Wright gravel stretch! Smooth asphalt pavement resumes into Fermont and the Labrador border.</desc><type>hazard</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.729326" lon="-67.413572"><name>🛑 Stop Sign — Before Single-Lane Bridge (QC-389)</name><desc>[Day 3] (hazard) ⚠️ Mandatory stop sign approaching narrow single-lane wilderness bridge on Route 389. Yield to oncoming heavy iron-ore haul trucks.</desc><type>hazard</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.584388" lon="-67.431434"><name>⚠️ Double Train Crossing (Cartier Railway QC-389)</name><desc>[Day 3] (hazard) ⚠️ Double industrial iron-ore railway crossing on Route 389. Cross tracks at a 90° angle and watch for wet steel rails.</desc><type>hazard</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.342896" lon="-67.390412"><name>⚠️ Train Crossing #1 (QC-389 / Iron Ore Railway)</name><desc>[Day 3] (hazard) Active Cartier / QNS&amp;L iron-ore railway grade crossing #1 across Route 389 (52.34290, -67.39041). Slow down and cross rails squarely.</desc><type>hazard</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.36297" lon="-67.385776"><name>⚠️ Train Crossing #2 (QC-389 / Iron Ore Railway)</name><desc>[Day 3] (hazard) Active Cartier / QNS&amp;L iron-ore railway grade crossing #2 across Route 389 (52.36297, -67.38578). Slow down and cross rails squarely.</desc><type>hazard</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.388552" lon="-67.374288"><name>⚠️ Train Crossing #3 (QC-389 / Iron Ore Railway)</name><desc>[Day 3] (hazard) Active Cartier / QNS&amp;L iron-ore railway grade crossing #3 across Route 389 (52.38855, -67.37429). Slow down and cross rails squarely.</desc><type>hazard</type></wpt>
