  <wpt lat="52.739139" lon="-67.412889"><name>⚠️ Train Crossing #10 (QC-389 / Iron Ore Railway)</name><desc>[Day 3] (hazard) Active Cartier / QNS&amp;L iron-ore railway grade crossing #10 across Route 389 (52.73914, -67.41289). Slow down and cross rails squarely.</desc><type>hazard</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.913255" lon="-67.025522"><name>⚠️ Train Crossing #11 (QC-389 / Iron Ore Railway)</name><desc>[Day 3] (hazard) Active Cartier / QNS&amp;L iron-ore railway grade crossing #11 across Route 389 (52.91325, -67.02552). Slow down and cross rails squarely.</desc><type>hazard</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.3292" lon="-68.1341"><name>Pourvoirie Relais Gabriel Restaurant (Hwy 389)</name><desc>[Day 3] (food) Iconic wilderness outfitter dining room at km 318 of Route 389 serving hot rider meals, soup, and coffee in the heart of the Côte-Nord.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.9463" lon="-66.9152"><name>Iron Rock Brewing Co. (Labrador City)</name><desc>[Day 3] (food) Labrador's premier craft brewery in Labrador City (118 Humphrey Rd) — great post-QC-389 celebration taproom and food stop.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.9448" lon="-66.9129"><name>Baba Q's Smoke &amp; Grill (Labrador City)</name><desc>[Day 3] (food) Authentic slow-smoked brisket, ribs, pulled pork, and hearty platters in Labrador City.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.2015" lon="-68.1842"><name>Tim Hortons (Baie-Comeau — Bd Laflèche)</name><desc>[Day 3] (coffee) 855 Bd Laflèche, Baie-Comeau, QC. Essential final Tim Hortons coffee &amp; breakfast stop before turning north onto Route 389 toward Manic-5!</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.6525" lon="-68.7385"><name>Belvédère Réservoir Manicouagan (QC-389 Viewpoint)</name><desc>[Day 3] (sight) Panoramic highway overlook beside the Manicouagan Reservoir ('Eye of Québec' annular impact crater lake) north of Manic-5 Dam.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.950649" lon="-68.139965"><name>Gagnon Airport (Former Mining Town Runway — QC-389)</name><desc>[Day 3] (sight) Abandoned airstrip and hauntingly flat highway corridor of the former iron-mining town of Gagnon (closed and dismantled in 1985) along Route 389.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.26816" lon="-67.647522"><name>QC-389 Off-Road Side-of-Road Viewpoint</name><desc>[Day 3] (sight) Elevated side-of-road gravel pull-off viewpoint overlooking the subarctic Côte-Nord valleys and lakes.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.320796" lon="-67.582709"><name>QC-389 Emergency Highway Telephone Booth</name><desc>[Day 3] (sight) Remote emergency satellite/landline highway telephone booth on Route 389 south of Fire Lake.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.344339" lon="-67.377745"><name>🚁 Drone Launch Spot: Fire Lake Iron Mine</name><desc>[Day 3] (sight) Designated roadside pullout to launch the drone for dramatic aerial footage of the ArcelorMittal Fire Lake open-pit iron mine and QC-389.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.776427" lon="-67.300992"><name>🚁 Drone Launch Spot: Mont-Wright Mega-Mine</name><desc>[Day 3] (sight) Prime roadside vantage point to fly the drone overlooking the colossal Mont-Wright open-pit iron ore mining complex near Fermont.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.818357" lon="-67.115868"><name>📸 Fermont Welcome Sign</name><desc>[Day 3] (sight) Photo-op stop at the town entrance sign for Fermont, QC (home of the famous 1.3 km wind-screening 'Le Mur-Écran' building).</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.86385" lon="-67.112159"><name>📸 Québec Provincial Border Sign (QC-389 / NL-500)</name><desc>[Day 3] (sight) Iconic 'Bonjour Québec' border sign at the 53rd parallel dividing Québec (Route 389) and Labrador (Route 500).</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.864452" lon="-67.111656"><name>📸 Welcome to Labrador Border Sign (South)</name><desc>[Day 3] (sight) Mandatory rider photo stop at the 'Welcome to Labrador / Bienvenue au Labrador' border monument entering Newfoundland &amp; Labrador!</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.865238" lon="-67.111567"><name>📸 Labrador Border Sign (North Pullout)</name><desc>[Day 3] (sight) Northern pullout side of the Québec–Labrador border crossing on Route 500.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.94501" lon="-66.973953"><name>Crystal Falls Hiking Trail (Labrador City)</name><desc>[Day 3] (hike) Scenic short hike overlooking cascading Crystal Falls between the Labrador border and Labrador City.</desc><type>hike</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.933453" lon="-66.935664"><name>Harrie Lake Trail (Labrador West)</name><desc>[Day 3] (hike) Peaceful boreal lakeside walking trail near Labrador City and Wabush.</desc><type>hike</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.95079" lon="-66.900059"><name>The Truck — Giant Terex Mining Dump Truck Display</name><desc>[Day 3] (attraction) Colossal retired open-pit iron ore haul truck on display in Labrador City — classic motorcycle scale photo-op!</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.95396" lon="-66.91792"><name>Smokey Mountain Ski &amp; Recreational Area</name><desc>[Day 3] (park) Labrador City's alpine ski hill and scenic high-point overlook just northwest of town.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.898039" lon="-66.881416"><name>Jean Lake Walking Trail (Wabush)</name><desc>[Day 3] (hike) 5.5 km groomed boardwalk and gravel walking trail looping around Jean Lake between Wabush and Labrador City.</desc><type>hike</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="53.305" lon="-60.325"><name>Royal Inn &amp; Suites (Goose Bay)</name><desc>[Day 4] (hotel-primary) Quiet, comfortable suites with kitchenettes in Happy Valley-Goose Bay. Secure parking, hot showers.</desc><type>hotel-primary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="53.3015" lon="-60.326"><name>Hotel North Two (Goose Bay)</name><desc>[Day 4] (hotel-secondary) Full service hotel with dining and heated indoor motorcycle parking options.</desc><type>hotel-secondary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="53.5333" lon="-64.0"><name>Churchill Falls Underground Hydro Plant</name><desc>[Day 4] (attraction) 5,428 MW underground power station hollowed out of solid Precambrian granite 305 m beneath the surface.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="53.5333" lon="-64.0"><name>Churchill Falls Gas &amp; Convenience</name><desc>[Day 4] (fuel) Km 238 on Route 500. Only fuel station between Lab City and Goose Bay. 87 reliable, 91 unreliable. Fill Africa Twin and dose Ducati.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="53.3017" lon="-60.3261"><name>Happy Valley-Goose Bay Esso/Irving Hub</name><desc>[Day 4] (fuel) MANDATORY: Fill main tanks + Rotopax + GL Armadillo bladder before embarking on Route 510!</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="53.35" lon="-62.15"><name>TLH 500 Minipi River Bladder Transfer Point</name><desc>[Day 4] (fuel) Midpoint rest area on TLH 500 (294 km gap) for auxiliary 91 fuel siphoning into Ducati.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="53.3038" lon="-60.3256"><name>Mamattuk Restaurant (Happy Valley-Goose Bay)</name><desc>[Day 4] (food) 2C Tenth St, Happy Valley-Goose Bay. Upscale Labrador dining featuring local wild game, Arctic char, and regional specialties.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="53.3061" lon="-60.3212"><name>Hotel North Restaurant (Happy Valley-Goose Bay)</name><desc>[Day 4] (food) Full-service restaurant inside Hotel North on Hamilton River Rd serving steaks, seafood, and hearty Labrador breakfasts.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.9458" lon="-66.9168"><name>Tim Hortons (Labrador City — Route 500)</name><desc>[Day 4] (coffee) 200 Route 500 (Carol Automart / Mall), Labrador City, NL. Hot coffee &amp; breakfast sandwiches before launching across the Trans-Labrador Highway.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.42" lon="-57.06"><name>Northern Light Inn (L'Anse-au-Clair)</name><desc>[Day 5] (hotel-primary) Rider-favorite coastal hotel 5 km from Blanc-Sablon ferry terminal. Warm rooms, seafood dining, early ferry staging.</desc><type>hotel-primary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.425" lon="-57.13"><name>Motel Blanc-Sablon</name><desc>[Day 5] (hotel-secondary) Waterfront motel right at the ferry terminal in Blanc-Sablon.</desc><type>hotel-secondary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.4572" lon="-56.8647"><name>Point Amour Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 5] (lighthouse) Tallest lighthouse in Atlantic Canada (33 m) and 2nd tallest in Canada; completed in 1857 guarding the treacherous Strait of Belle Isle.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.733" lon="-56.425"><name>Tracey Hill 700-Step Overlook (Red Bay)</name><desc>[Day 5] (hike) 700 wooden boardwalk stairs climbing Tracey Hill behind the Red Bay UNESCO Basque Whaling Station. Panoramic view over Saddle Island icebergs.</desc><type>hike</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.465" lon="-56.865"><name>L'Anse Amour 7,500-Year Burial Mound</name><desc>[Day 5] (attraction) The oldest known human-constructed funeral burial mound in North America (Maritime Archaic Indigenous culture, 5500 BCE), marked by a stone cairn.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.455" lon="-56.868"><name>HMS Raleigh 1922 Shipwreck &amp; Raleigh Trail</name><desc>[Day 5] (attraction) Remains of the 600-ft British Royal Navy heavy cruiser HMS Raleigh that ran aground in blinding fog in 1922 beneath Point Amour. Steam boilers visible on beach.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.7333" lon="-56.4167"><name>Red Bay Basque Whaling Station (UNESCO)</name><desc>[Day 5] (attraction) UNESCO World Heritage Site. 16th-century Basque whaling headquarters in North America. Sunken galleons &amp; tryworks rendering ovens.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="53.0" lon="-57.8"><name>CRITICAL: Route 510 Mid-Stage Bladder Transfer</name><desc>[Day 5] (fuel) 405 KM ZERO-SERVICE GAP. At Km 240, transfer 1.5-2.0 gallons from Africa Twin Armadillo bladder into Ducati Multistrada V2S.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.538" lon="-56.297"><name>Port Hope Simpson Gas Bar</name><desc>[Day 5] (fuel) Km 405 from Goose Bay. Critical remote fuel stop on TLH 510. 87 Octane ONLY. Pour Africa Twin bladder into Ducati.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="52.3117" lon="-55.835"><name>Mary's Harbour North Atlantic</name><desc>[Day 5] (fuel) Convenient coastal fuel station on Route 510.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.4242" lon="-57.1472"><name>Blanc-Sablon Ultramar</name><desc>[Day 5] (fuel) Near ferry terminal. Top off before boarding morning MV Qajaq W ferry to Newfoundland.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.515" lon="-56.83"><name>L'Anse-au-Loup North Atlantic</name><desc>[Day 5] (fuel) Southern Labrador coastal strategic backup station 25 km north of Blanc-Sablon.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.4208" lon="-57.0628"><name>Northern Light Inn Dining Room (L'Anse-au-Clair)</name><desc>[Day 5] (food) Welcoming Strait of Belle Isle dining room right at the Labrador/Newfoundland gateway serving cod tongues, seafood chowder, and roast turkey dinners.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="53.3072" lon="-60.3285"><name>Tim Hortons (Happy Valley-Goose Bay)</name><desc>[Day 5] (coffee) 356 Hamilton River Rd, Happy Valley-Goose Bay, NL. Early morning coffee stop before the 608 km ride south to the Strait of Belle Isle.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.5833" lon="-55.5333"><name>Snorri Cabins / Valhalla Lodge (Hay Cove)</name><desc>[Day 6] (hotel-primary) Authentic turf-roofed and wooden rustic Viking cabins 2 km from L'Anse aux Meadows. Full kitchen, private deck, ocean vistas.</desc><type>hotel-primary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.365" lon="-55.605"><name>Haven Inn (St. Anthony)</name><desc>[Day 6] (hotel-secondary) Modern hotel in St. Anthony with full dining, comfortable beds, and full amenities.</desc><type>hotel-secondary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.6315" lon="-55.903"><name>Cape Norman Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 6] (lighthouse) Towering cliffside light marking the absolute northernmost tip of the island of Newfoundland; sweeps Strait of Belle Isle iceberg alley.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.3608" lon="-55.5539"><name>Fishing Point Lighthouse (Fox Point Light - St. Anthony)</name><desc>[Day 6] (lighthouse) Famous red-and-white beacon perched atop jagged coastal cliffs at Fishing Point in St. Anthony. Prime iceberg watching and marine trails.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.605" lon="-55.76"><name>Burnt Cape Ecological Reserve (Arctic Barrens)</name><desc>[Day 6] (hike) Alien subarctic landscape near Raleigh resembling the surface of Mars. Coastal limestone sea arches, wave-carved caves, and rare arctic plants.</desc><type>hike</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.5956" lon="-55.5314"><name>L'Anse aux Meadows (UNESCO Viking Settlement)</name><desc>[Day 6] (attraction) Only confirmed Norse Viking site in North America (circa 1000 AD). Authentic turf houses, blacksmith shop, and archaeological museum.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.363" lon="-55.599"><name>Grenfell Historic Properties &amp; Museum (St. Anthony)</name><desc>[Day 6] (attraction) Historic mission headquarters of Dr. Wilfred Grenfell who brought modern medicine to remote Newfoundland and Labrador. Historic home and museum.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.2" lon="-56.7667"><name>St. Barbe North Atlantic</name><desc>[Day 6] (fuel) Immediately upon disembarking ferry in NL. Convenient top-off before riding Viking Trail.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.57" lon="-55.73"><name>Raleigh Gas Bar</name><desc>[Day 6] (fuel) Route 437 backup gas bar near Burnt Cape Ecological Reserve.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.365" lon="-55.598"><name>St. Anthony Irving / North Atlantic Hub</name><desc>[Day 6] (fuel) Northern Peninsula commercial fuel hub with reliable 91 Premium.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.425" lon="-57.135"><name>Blanc-Sablon to St. Barbe Ferry (MV Qajaq W)</name><desc>[Day 6] (ferry) 90-minute marine ferry across the Strait of Belle Isle into Newfoundland. Chocks and heavy-duty straps provided for motorcycles.</desc><type>ferry</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.3688" lon="-55.5924"><name>Rudder's Restaurant &amp; Pub (St. Anthony)</name><desc>[Day 6] (food) Waterfront harbour pub in St. Anthony overlooking Iceberg Alley, famous for pan-fried cod, moose burgers, and partridgeberry desserts.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.3609" lon="-55.5568"><name>Lightkeepers Café (Fishing Point, St. Anthony)</name><desc>[Day 6] (food) Perched at Fishing Point Park beneath Fox Point Lighthouse — spectacular whale &amp; iceberg viewing deck with fresh seafood chowder and fishcakes.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.3694" lon="-55.5951"><name>The Great Viking Feast Dinner Theatre (St. Anthony)</name><desc>[Day 6] (food) Interactive 11th-century Norse sod-house dinner theatre in St. Anthony featuring Viking comedy, mead, and traditional Newfoundland dishes.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.3712" lon="-55.5968"><name>Tim Hortons (St. Anthony)</name><desc>[Day 6] (coffee) West St, St. Anthony, NL. Northernmost Tim Hortons in Newfoundland — great warm-up stop after visiting L'Anse aux Meadows &amp; Iceberg Alley.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.3642" lon="-55.5845"><name>Grenfell Historic Properties (St. Anthony)</name><desc>[Day 6] (attraction) Museum, historic home, and interpretive centre honoring medical missionary Sir Wilfred Grenfell in St. Anthony.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.3605" lon="-55.5558"><name>Fox Point Lighthouse (Fishing Point, St. Anthony)</name><desc>[Day 6] (lighthouse) Iconic red-and-white hexagonal lighthouse perched on the dramatic cliffs of Fishing Point at the entrance to St. Anthony Harbour.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.5833" lon="-55.5333"><name>Snorri Cabins / Valhalla Lodge (Hay Cove) - Night 2</name><desc>[Day 7] (hotel-primary) Night 2 in the Viking cabins. Relax around the woodstove after exploring Norstead and St. Anthony.</desc><type>hotel-primary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.365" lon="-55.605"><name>Haven Inn (St. Anthony) - Night 2</name><desc>[Day 7] (hotel-secondary) St. Anthony motor inn fallback for Day 7.</desc><type>hotel-secondary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.6088" lon="-55.6232"><name>Cape Onion / Quirpon Island Lookout</name><desc>[Day 7] (lighthouse) Rugged clifftop headland looking out across the Atlantic toward Quirpon Island Light (1860) and iceberg drift channels.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.599" lon="-55.52"><name>Norstead Viking Village &amp; Snorri Knarr Ship</name><desc>[Day 7] (attraction) Living history Viking trading port featuring the 54-foot replica knarr merchant ship 'Snorri', axe throwing, and forge.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.5928" lon="-55.5312"><name>The Norseman Restaurant (L'Anse aux Meadows)</name><desc>[Day 7] (food) Harbourside fine dining steps from L'Anse aux Meadows UNESCO Viking site — renowned for bakeapple cheesecake, halibut, and iceberg beer.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.5098" lon="-55.4662"><name>The Daily Catch (St. Lunaire-Griquet)</name><desc>[Day 7] (food) 214 Main St, St. Lunaire-Griquet. Beloved Great Northern Peninsula seafood restaurant serving fresh-off-the-boat Atlantic cod, snow crab, and lobster.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.5042" lon="-55.4695"><name>Café Nymphe — The Dark Tickle Company (St. Lunaire-Griquet)</name><desc>[Day 7] (food) 75 Main St, St. Lunaire-Griquet. Economuseum and wild-berry café specializing in bakeapple (cloudberry), partridgeberry, and crowberry treats &amp; espresso.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.5561" lon="-55.7364"><name>Burnt Cape Café (Raleigh, NL-430)</name><desc>[Day 7] (food) Home-cooked Newfoundland meals, toutons, cod au gratin, and fresh-baked bread in the coastal fishing village of Raleigh.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.5472" lon="-55.5245"><name>Northern Delight Restaurant (Gunners Cove)</name><desc>[Day 7] (food) Main Street, Gunners Cove. Cozy Viking Trail stop for breakfast, fish &amp; chips, moose soup, and homemade berry pies.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.56" lon="-57.88"><name>Gros Morne / Norris Point KOA Holiday</name><desc>[Day 8] (hotel-primary) Full-service KOA at Route 430 junction in Gros Morne. Commercial laundromat to reset riding gear, heated pool, hot showers, bike wash.</desc><type>hotel-primary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.5936" lon="-57.9172"><name>Ocean View Hotel (Rocky Harbour)</name><desc>[Day 8] (hotel-secondary) Premier waterfront hotel fallback in Rocky Harbour with live music and restaurant.</desc><type>hotel-secondary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.585" lon="-57.9"><name>Gros Morne National Park (Rocky Harbour)</name><desc>[Day 8] (park) UNESCO World Heritage Site with dramatic glacial fjords, Tablelands, and coastal trails.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.56" lon="-57.88"><name>Gros Morne KOA Holiday Park Grounds</name><desc>[Day 8] (park) Full-amenity outdoor park setting with bike wash, pool, and laundromat.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.703" lon="-57.411"><name>Pointe Riche Lighthouse &amp; Limestone Barrens</name><desc>[Day 8] (lighthouse) Historic 1892 octagonal wooden pepperpot lighthouse on dramatic fossil-rich limestone sea barrens in Port au Choix.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.6055" lon="-57.958"><name>Lobster Cove Head Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 8] (lighthouse) Historic 1897 wooden light marking the entrance to Bonne Bay in Gros Morne National Park; panoramic sunset vistas and coastal trails.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.682" lon="-57.962"><name>Green Point Geological Golden Spike (GSSP)</name><desc>[Day 8] (hike) UN Global Boundary Stratotype Section and Point (GSSP). Layered coastal shale cliffs marking 500-million-year-old geological boundary with graptolite fossils.</desc><type>hike</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.493" lon="-58.125"><name>Trout River Eastern Point Clifftop Trail</name><desc>[Day 8] (hike) Spectacular 30-minute wooden stairway trail rising to open grassy cliff headlands where sheep graze above crashing Gulf swells.</desc><type>hike</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.831" lon="-57.872"><name>Broom Point Traditional Cod Fishing Premises</name><desc>[Day 8] (attraction) Preserved 1960s inshore cod-fishing family cabin and workshop in Gros Morne. Restored wooden dories, drying flakes, and living history.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.61" lon="-57.17"><name>Hawke's Bay North Atlantic</name><desc>[Day 8] (fuel) Route 430 Viking Trail backup station with 91 Premium.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="50.708" lon="-57.365"><name>Port au Choix Co-op Fuel</name><desc>[Day 8] (fuel) Convenient fuel station on way to Point Riche Lighthouse.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.5933" lon="-57.915"><name>Rocky Harbour Irving</name><desc>[Day 8] (fuel) Gros Morne National Park central fuel, convenience, air pump.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="51.08" lon="-56.88"><name>Plum Point Gas Bar</name><desc>[Day 8] (fuel) Route 430 Viking Trail coastal backup station between St. Barbe and Hawke's Bay.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.98" lon="-57.7"><name>Parson's Pond North Atlantic</name><desc>[Day 8] (fuel) Northern Gros Morne coastal backup station along Route 430.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.5914" lon="-57.9168"><name>Java Jack's Restaurant &amp; Gallery (Rocky Harbour)</name><desc>[Day 8] (food) Acclaimed culinary gem in the heart of Gros Morne National Park (Rocky Harbour) — creative Newfoundland seafood, espresso, and local art.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.5902" lon="-57.9189"><name>Ocean View Bistro &amp; Dining (Rocky Harbour)</name><desc>[Day 8] (food) Harbourfront dining room overlooking Bonne Bay in Rocky Harbour serving fresh Atlantic lobster, cod, and Newfoundland entertainment.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.6833" lon="-57.85"><name>Green Point Campground (Gros Morne NP)</name><desc>[Day 9] (hotel-primary) World-class coastal drive-in campground in Gros Morne perched on seaside bluffs overlooking the Gulf of St. Lawrence. Ocean sunset, campfire surf.</desc><type>hotel-primary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.61" lon="-57.87"><name>Berry Hill Campground (Gros Morne NP)</name><desc>[Day 9] (hotel-secondary) Gros Morne central campground in sheltered boreal forest near Rocky Harbour.</desc><type>hotel-secondary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.6833" lon="-57.85"><name>Green Point Coastal Bluffs (Gros Morne NP)</name><desc>[Day 9] (park) Seaside bluff camping overlooking crashing ocean waves and gravel beach.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.61" lon="-57.87"><name>Berry Hill Boreal Park Grounds (Gros Morne NP)</name><desc>[Day 9] (park) Deep boreal forest camping sheltered beneath Gros Morne Mountain.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.5028" lon="-57.9189"><name>Woody Point Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 9] (lighthouse) Iconic 1919 square pyramid wooden pepperpot tower guarding the south entrance to Bonne Bay and the Tablelands fjord in Gros Morne NP.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.498" lon="-57.925"><name>Woody Point Gas Bar</name><desc>[Day 9] (fuel) Bonne Bay / Tablelands backup gas outpost.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.48" lon="-58.12"><name>Trout River Gas Bar</name><desc>[Day 9] (fuel) Western coastal terminus backup station on the Tablelands spur.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.475" lon="-57.964"><name>The Tablelands (Earth's Mantle)</name><desc>[Day 9] (sight) Rare barren orange landscape of exposed oceanic crust and Earth's mantle pushed up by continental drift.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.1804" lon="-57.4192"><name>Deer Lake Irving Big Stop Restaurant (Deer Lake)</name><desc>[Day 9] (food) 62 Trans-Canada Hwy, Deer Lake. Classic rider pit stop with huge country breakfasts, hot turkey sandwiches, and fish &amp; chips right at the Route 430 junction.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.1765" lon="-57.4318"><name>Off The Hook Fish &amp; Chips (Deer Lake)</name><desc>[Day 9] (food) 37 Old Bonne Bay Rd, Deer Lake. Crispy golden beer-battered Newfoundland cod &amp; hand-cut fries.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.9518" lon="-57.9482"><name>Shipyard Eatery / Boomstick Brewing (Corner Brook)</name><desc>[Day 9] (food) 55 West St, Corner Brook (inside Hew &amp; Draw Hotel). Craft brewery and scratch kitchen serving elevated gastropub fare.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.9502" lon="-57.9465"><name>Jennifer's Restaurant (Corner Brook)</name><desc>[Day 9] (food) 48 Broadway, Corner Brook. Long-standing local favourite for prime rib, stuffed cod, and classic Newfoundland hospitality.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.1792" lon="-57.4215"><name>Tim Hortons (Deer Lake — Trans-Canada Hwy 1)</name><desc>[Day 9] (coffee) Trans-Canada Hwy &amp; Route 430 Junction, Deer Lake, NL. Rider hub right at the Viking Trail exit.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.9435" lon="-57.9312"><name>Starbucks (Corner Brook — Murphy Square)</name><desc>[Day 9] (coffee) 44 Maple Valley Rd, Corner Brook, NL. Espresso and pastry stop in Corner Brook.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.9488" lon="-57.9432"><name>Corner Brook Stream Trail</name><desc>[Day 9] (hike) Lush gorge boardwalk, waterfalls, and salmon stream trail winding right through the heart of Corner Brook.</desc><type>hike</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.575" lon="-59.136"><name>Marine Atlantic Overnight Ferry (Private 2-Berth Stateroom Cabin)</name><desc>[Day 10] (hotel-primary) Private 2-berth en-suite stateroom aboard MV Highlanders / MV Blue Puttees. Boarding 21:45, sailing 23:45 across Cabot Strait to North Sydney arriving 07:00 AM.</desc><type>hotel-primary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.578" lon="-59.145"><name>Hotel Port aux Basques (Ferry Staging Backup)</name><desc>[Day 10] (hotel-secondary) Comfortable hotel 2 minutes from the Marine Atlantic ferry terminal dock; ideal staging backup if sailing is delayed.</desc><type>hotel-secondary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.9" lon="-59.408"><name>Cape Anguille Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 10] (lighthouse) Historic 1905 light marking the absolute westernmost point of the island of Newfoundland; dramatic Gulf of St. Lawrence ocean cliffs.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.618" lon="-59.293"><name>Cape Ray Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 10] (lighthouse) Established 1871; historic landfall for the first transatlantic telegraph cable from Ireland; sweeps Cabot Strait and maritime trade route.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.715" lon="-59.325"><name>Wreckhouse Extreme Winds Corridor</name><desc>[Day 10] (attraction) Legendary coastal funnel where southeastern mountain gusts exceed 200 km/h, famously blowing trains off their tracks.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="49.1728" lon="-57.4328"><name>Deer Lake Irving Big Stop</name><desc>[Day 10] (fuel) Major junction of Viking Trail (NL-430) and Trans-Canada Hwy 1.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.95" lon="-57.945"><name>Corner Brook Irving Big Stop</name><desc>[Day 10] (fuel) Trans-Canada Hwy 1 full service hub with 91 Premium.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.512" lon="-58.448"><name>Stephenville Crossing Esso</name><desc>[Day 10] (fuel) Mid-stage fuel top-off heading down the west coast.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.5717" lon="-59.1367"><name>Port aux Basques Irving</name><desc>[Day 10] (fuel) Fill tanks before checking in for overnight Marine Atlantic ferry crossing to Nova Scotia.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.835" lon="-59.18"><name>Doyles Esso (Codroy Valley)</name><desc>[Day 10] (fuel) Trans-Canada Hwy 1 backup station 30 km north of Port aux Basques ferry dock.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.5739" lon="-59.1367"><name>Marine Atlantic Port aux Basques Overnight Ferry</name><desc>[Day 10] (ferry) Marine Atlantic 7-hour overnight marine ferry across the Cabot Strait to North Sydney aboard MV Highlanders. Departs 23:45, arrives 07:00 AM.</desc><type>ferry</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.5762" lon="-59.1468"><name>Alma's Family Restaurant (Channel-Port aux Basques)</name><desc>[Day 10] (food) 27 Grand Bay Rd, Channel-Port aux Basques. Homestyle pre-ferry dinner or breakfast spot minutes from the Marine Atlantic terminal.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.5785" lon="-59.1482"><name>Tim Hortons (Channel-Port aux Basques)</name><desc>[Day 10] (coffee) Grand Bay Rd, Channel-Port aux Basques, NL. Right next to the Marine Atlantic Ferry staging terminal.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.68" lon="-60.4"><name>Broad Cove Campground (Cape Breton Highlands NP)</name><desc>[Day 11] (hotel-primary) Spectacular oceanfront National Park campground in Ingonish directly on the Cabot Trail. Sandy ocean beach, hot showers, flush toilets, campfire pits.</desc><type>hotel-primary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.655" lon="-60.395"><name>Keltic Lodge at the Highlands (Ingonish)</name><desc>[Day 11] (hotel-secondary) Historic clifftop luxury resort fallback on Middle Head Peninsula.</desc><type>hotel-secondary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.64" lon="-60.395"><name>Cape Breton Highlands National Park (East Entrance)</name><desc>[Day 11] (park) Parks Canada Atlantic jewel where mountains meet the sea.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.68" lon="-60.4"><name>Broad Cove Ocean Beach Park (Cape Breton Highlands NP)</name><desc>[Day 11] (park) Ocean beach park campground with direct sandy beach access and fire pits.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.812" lon="-60.32"><name>Neil's Harbour Lighthouse &amp; Chowder House</name><desc>[Day 11] (lighthouse) 1899 coastal wooden lighthouse serving fresh ice cream and Atlantic seafood chowder perched over crashing Cabot Trail surf.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.903" lon="-60.355"><name>White Point Unknown Sailor Clifftop Trail</name><desc>[Day 11] (hike) Rugged coastal path out onto an isolated rocky headland jutting into the Atlantic. Sea bird colonies and the solitary white cross of the Unknown Sailor's grave.</desc><type>hike</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.777" lon="-60.331"><name>Black Brook Cove Waterfall &amp; Ocean Beach</name><desc>[Day 11] (hike) Spectacular Atlantic ocean beach in Cape Breton Highlands where a freshwater mountain brook and waterfall cascade over sea cliffs onto the sand.</desc><type>hike</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.273" lon="-60.5985"><name>The Gaelic College / Colaisde na Gàidhlig (St. Ann's)</name><desc>[Day 11] (attraction) Historic Gaelic cultural learning institution founded in 1938 at the start of the Cabot Trail in St. Ann's; preserves Highland Scottish heritage and Celtic arts.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.2067" lon="-60.2533"><name>North Sydney Esso</name><desc>[Day 11] (fuel) Directly outside ferry terminal dock. Start Cabot Trail on 100% full tanks.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.255" lon="-60.44"><name>Boularderie Irving (Hwy 105)</name><desc>[Day 11] (fuel) Hwy 105 service station before Seal Island Bridge and Kelly's Mountain.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.64" lon="-60.4"><name>Ingonish Petro-Canada / Shell</name><desc>[Day 11] (fuel) Cabot Trail East gateway and Broad Cove campground fuel hub.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.6" lon="-60.4167"><name>Cape Smokey Look-off &amp; Gondola</name><desc>[Day 11] (sight) Thrilling coastal hairpin climb to high mountain look-off overlooking Ingonish and the Atlantic Ocean.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.3085" lon="-60.5318"><name>The Chanterelle Country Inn &amp; Restaurant (Cabot Trail)</name><desc>[Day 11] (food) Scenic farm-to-table dining along the Cabot Trail between Baddeck and Ingonish overlooking St. Ann's Bay.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.6852" lon="-60.3765"><name>Coastal Restaurant &amp; Pub (Ingonish)</name><desc>[Day 11] (food) 36404 Cabot Trail, Ingonish. Famous home of the 'aranac' burger, Digby scallops, and Cape Breton craft beer.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.2085" lon="-60.2542"><name>Tim Hortons (North Sydney — Ferry Terminal Approach)</name><desc>[Day 11] (coffee) 119 King St, North Sydney, NS. First coffee stop off the morning ferry arrival from Newfoundland before riding the Cabot Trail.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.1012" lon="-60.7548"><name>Tim Hortons (Baddeck — Cabot Trail Gateway)</name><desc>[Day 11] (coffee) 9025 Trans-Canada Hwy 105, Baddeck, NS. Gateway coffee stop at the start/finish of the Cabot Trail loop.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.64" lon="-60.98"><name>Chéticamp Campground (Cape Breton Highlands NP)</name><desc>[Day 12] (hotel-primary) Tucked in the mountain valley at the western park entrance of the Cabot Trail. Hot showers, walking distance to Chéticamp village.</desc><type>hotel-primary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.627" lon="-61.01"><name>Laurie's Motor Inn (Chéticamp)</name><desc>[Day 12] (hotel-secondary) Comfortable Acadian motor inn on the Cabot Trail in Chéticamp; restaurant, lounge, and room-front bike parking.</desc><type>hotel-secondary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.64" lon="-60.98"><name>Chéticamp Mountain Valley Park (Highlands NP)</name><desc>[Day 12] (park) Acadian valley park campsite near the Skyline Trail and French Mountain.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.903" lon="-60.46"><name>St. Paul Island Southwest Lighthouse (Dingwall)</name><desc>[Day 12] (lighthouse) Rare 1915 cylindrical cast iron lighthouse relocated from the treacherous 'Graveyard of the Gulf' (St. Paul Island) to Dingwall Harbour.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.663" lon="-61.025"><name>Chéticamp Enragée Point Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 12] (lighthouse) Historic coastal beacon on Chéticamp Island overlooking the Gulf of St. Lawrence and Acadian fishing fleet.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.745" lon="-60.875"><name>Skyline Trail Boardwalk Hike</name><desc>[Day 12] (hike) World-famous 2-hour coastal hike to a dramatic wooden boardwalk looking down on the Cabot Trail hairpins, crashing ocean, and grazing moose.</desc><type>hike</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.903" lon="-60.465"><name>Dingwall Gas Bar &amp; Convenience</name><desc>[Day 12] (fuel) Aspy Bay backup fuel station before Meat Cove clifftop spur.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.64" lon="-61.0"><name>Chéticamp Co-op Gas Bar</name><desc>[Day 12] (fuel) Western coastal exit of the Cabot Trail. 91 Premium available.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.885" lon="-60.505"><name>Cape North Co-op Gas Bar</name><desc>[Day 12] (fuel) Northern Cabot Trail junction backup station before Meat Cove spur.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.0264" lon="-60.5578"><name>Meat Cove Clifftop Adventure Spur &amp; Chowder Hut</name><desc>[Day 12] (sight) The wild northernmost tip of Nova Scotia. 29 km spur ending with an 8 km clifftop ocean track and clifftop chowder hut.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.73" lon="-60.88"><name>French Mountain Switchbacks</name><desc>[Day 12] (sight) The signature postcard hairpins of the Cabot Trail carved into sheer mountain coastal bluffs.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.635" lon="-61.005"><name>Aucoin Bakery (Chéticamp)</name><desc>[Day 12] (sight) Famous Acadian bakery operating since 1955. Traditional meat pies, pastries, and breads.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.6312" lon="-61.0108"><name>Le Gabriel Restaurant &amp; Lounge (Chéticamp)</name><desc>[Day 12] (food) 15424 Cabot Trail, Chéticamp. Landmark Acadian seafood restaurant featuring snow crab, lobster dinners, Acadian chicken fricot, and live fiddle music.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.6378" lon="-61.0072"><name>L'Abri Café, Restaurant et Bar (Chéticamp)</name><desc>[Day 12] (food) 15549 Cabot Trail, Chéticamp. Vibrant coastal bistro overlooking the Gulf of St. Lawrence — lobster rolls, fish tacos, craft cocktails, and espresso.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.6265" lon="-61.0138"><name>Harbour Restaurant &amp; Bar (Chéticamp)</name><desc>[Day 12] (food) 15289 Cabot Trail, Chéticamp. Dockside patio right on the Chéticamp boardwalk with fresh lobster, haddock, and harbour views.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.6295" lon="-61.0121"><name>Mr. Chicken / Last Chance Sandwich Stop (Chéticamp)</name><desc>[Day 12] (food) Quick Cabot Trail sandwich, wrap, and picnic lunch stop in Chéticamp before riding the western coastal cliffs.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.6242" lon="-61.0152"><name>Restaurant Évangéline (Chéticamp)</name><desc>[Day 12] (food) 15212 Cabot Trail, Chéticamp. Traditional Acadian home cooking, meat pies, fish &amp; chips, and homemade coconut cream pie.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.6345" lon="-61.0091"><name>Seafood Stop (Chéticamp)</name><desc>[Day 12] (food) Fresh local Cape Breton lobster, crab, chowder, and takeaway seafood along the Chéticamp harbour strip.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.6278" lon="-61.0131"><name>The Doryman Pub &amp; Grill (Chéticamp)</name><desc>[Day 12] (food) 15328 Cabot Trail, Chéticamp. Legendary Cape Breton live-music tavern and grill — world-famous Saturday afternoon &amp; evening ceilidh fiddle sessions.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.495" lon="-63.402"><name>Cavendish Campground (Prince Edward Island National Park)</name><desc>[Day 13] (hotel-primary) Pristine Parks Canada oceanfront campground directly on the Gulf of St. Lawrence red sand dunes and sandstone cliffs. Walking access to Cavendish Beach and 3 min to Anne of Green Gables.</desc><type>hotel-primary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.488" lon="-63.388"><name>Kindred Spirits Country Inn &amp; Cottages (Cavendish)</name><desc>[Day 13] (hotel-secondary) Charming country estate nestled beside the Anne of Green Gables homestead in Cavendish; heated outdoor pool.</desc><type>hotel-secondary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.495" lon="-63.402"><name>Prince Edward Island National Park (Cavendish Beach)</name><desc>[Day 13] (park) Oceanfront National Park on the Gulf of St. Lawrence red sand dunes and sandstone cliffs.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.435" lon="-61.108"><name>Margaree Harbour Range Lights</name><desc>[Day 13] (lighthouse) Twin 1900 Acadian wooden range lights guiding fishing schooners into the mouth of the Margaree River salmon estuary.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.215" lon="-63.488"><name>Victoria Harbour Range Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 13] (lighthouse) 1879 wooden square tapered tower in the historic artisan fishing and seafaring village of Victoria-by-the-Sea on PEI's south shore.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.524" lon="-63.504"><name>Cape Tryon Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 13] (lighthouse) Iconic lighthouse perched on 110-foot vertical red sandstone cliffs overlooking Gulf of St. Lawrence; inspiration for L.M. Montgomery's Four Winds Light.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.46" lon="-63.292"><name>North Rustico Harbour Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 13] (lighthouse) 1876 square pyramid pepperpot lighthouse with attached keeper's dwelling in a classic active PEI lobster fishing harbour.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.431" lon="-63.146"><name>Covehead Harbour Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 13] (lighthouse) Beloved 1975 pepperpot lighthouse nestled among the rolling coastal sand dunes of Prince Edward Island National Park.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.058" lon="-63.048"><name>Point Prim Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 13] (lighthouse) Built 1845, the oldest lighthouse on Prince Edward Island and one of only a few round brick lighthouses in Canada.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.619" lon="-64.387"><name>West Point Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 13] (lighthouse) PEI's tallest lighthouse (69 ft), famous for its striking black-and-white horizontal stripes and Northumberland Strait sunsets.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4917" lon="-63.385"><name>Anne of Green Gables Heritage Place</name><desc>[Day 13] (attraction) Historic 19th-century Victorian farmstead, Haunted Wood trail, and Lovers Lane that inspired L.M. Montgomery's classic novel.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.505" lon="-63.468"><name>L.M. Montgomery's Birthplace (New London)</name><desc>[Day 13] (attraction) Cozy white-and-green farmhouse in New London where author Lucy Maud Montgomery was born in 1874. Displays replica wedding dress and scrapbooks.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.521" lon="-63.535"><name>Anne of Green Gables Museum at Silver Bush</name><desc>[Day 13] (attraction) Historic Campbell family homestead where Montgomery was married. Features Matthew's carriage rides and views over the Lake of Shining Waters.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.525" lon="-63.538"><name>Lake of Shining Waters (Park Corner)</name><desc>[Day 13] (attraction) Pristine freshwater pond glistening behind the coastal barrier dunes immortalized by Montgomery as 'The Lake of Shining Waters'.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.516" lon="-63.513"><name>French River Overlook &amp; Fishing Cove</name><desc>[Day 13] (attraction) Postcard-perfect PEI landscape of rolling emerald green potato fields sloping down to colorful fishing shacks on the quiet river inlet.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.498" lon="-63.415"><name>Cavendish Beach Sandstone Sea Stacks</name><desc>[Day 13] (attraction) Towering red sandstone arches, caves, and barrier dunes glowing fiery red in the late afternoon sun along the Cavendish coastline.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.486" lon="-63.382"><name>Site of L.M. Montgomery's Cavendish Home</name><desc>[Day 13] (attraction) Peaceful wooded homestead where Montgomery was raised by her grandparents and wrote Anne of Green Gables. Path through apple orchard.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.645" lon="-61.405"><name>Port Hastings Irving</name><desc>[Day 13] (fuel) Canso Causeway gateway full service station with 91 Premium.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.58" lon="-62.64"><name>New Glasgow Irving</name><desc>[Day 13] (fuel) Trans-Canada Hwy 104 full service hub on mainland Nova Scotia.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.255" lon="-63.685"><name>Borden-Carleton Gateway Shell (PEI)</name><desc>[Day 13] (fuel) Directly at the PEI landing of Confederation Bridge.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.488" lon="-63.385"><name>Cavendish Shell</name><desc>[Day 13] (fuel) Route 6 PEI central North Shore station near Anne of Green Gables.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.62" lon="-61.98"><name>Antigonish Shell</name><desc>[Day 13] (fuel) Trans-Canada Hwy 104 mainland NS backup station between Canso Causeway and New Glasgow.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.645" lon="-61.415"><name>Canso Causeway (Cape Breton Island Gateway)</name><desc>[Day 13] (ferry) Massive rock-fill causeway carrying Highway 104 across the Strait of Canso connecting mainland Nova Scotia to Cape Breton Island.</desc><type>ferry</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.155" lon="-63.812"><name>Confederation Bridge (Inbound Toll-Free Crossing)</name><desc>[Day 13] (ferry) 12.9 km curved marine highway bridge spanning Northumberland Strait from New Brunswick onto PEI. 100% modified asphalt, zero grates, 100% toll-free inbound!</desc><type>ferry</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.2348" lon="-63.1262"><name>The Old Triangle Irish Alehouse (Sydney / Charlottetown)</name><desc>[Day 13] (food) 75 University Ave, Charlottetown (and Charlotte St, Sydney). Authentic Irish pub fare, boxties, Guinness, and live East Coast music.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.0518" lon="-62.9982"><name>Point Prim Chowder House (Point Prim, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 13] (food) 2150 Point Prim Rd, Belfast, PEI. Waterfront gem right at Point Prim Lighthouse off the Wood Islands ferry — world-class seafood chowder and lobster rolls.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.6185" lon="-61.3512"><name>Tim Hortons (Port Hawkesbury — Canso Causeway)</name><desc>[Day 13] (coffee) 632 Reeves St, Port Hawkesbury, NS. Coffee stop right after crossing the Canso Causeway onto mainland Nova Scotia.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.5742" lon="-62.6468"><name>Starbucks (New Glasgow, NS — Highland Square)</name><desc>[Day 13] (coffee) 699 Westville Rd, New Glasgow, NS. Espresso stop en route to the Caribou–Wood Islands PEI ferry.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.0504" lon="-62.9992"><name>Point Prim Lighthouse (Point Prim, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 13] (lighthouse) Built in 1845 — PEI's oldest lighthouse and one of only two round brick lighthouses in Canada, minutes from the Wood Islands ferry.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.0068" lon="-62.4592"><name>Cape Bear Lighthouse &amp; Marconi Station (Murray Harbour, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 13] (lighthouse) 1881 cliffside lighthouse on southeastern PEI where Canadian wireless operators first received the distress call from the sinking RMS Titanic in 1912.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.598" lon="-64.952"><name>Fundy National Park (Headquarters Campground)</name><desc>[Day 14] (hotel-primary) Perched on seaside bluffs overlooking the Bay of Fundy above Alma harbor. Heated washrooms, hot showers, walk down to fresh Fundy lobster.</desc><type>hotel-primary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.6025" lon="-64.9458"><name>Parkland Village Inn (Alma / Fundy)</name><desc>[Day 14] (hotel-secondary) Cozy seaside inn fallback directly across from the harbor in Alma.</desc><type>hotel-secondary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.598" lon="-64.952"><name>Fundy National Park (Headquarters Bayview)</name><desc>[Day 14] (park) Clifftop park campground above Alma harbor overlooking the highest tides on Earth.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.319" lon="-63.61"><name>Seacow Head Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 14] (lighthouse) Built 1863; one of PEI's oldest octagonal wooden lights; famous feature in 'Road to Avonlea' perched above red sandstone sea arches.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.132" lon="-63.778"><name>Cape Tormentine Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 14] (lighthouse) Historic light marking the former ice-boat and rail-ferry terminal crossing the Northumberland Strait to PEI.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.155" lon="-63.812"><name>Cape Jourimain Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 14] (lighthouse) 1870 octagonal wood lighthouse standing watch beside the massive spans of Confederation Bridge in Cape Jourimain Nature Centre.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.594" lon="-64.783"><name>Cape Enrage Lighthouse &amp; Cliffs</name><desc>[Day 14] (lighthouse) Built 1838 atop 150-foot jagged cliffs thrust into the Bay of Fundy; faces the most powerful 50-foot tidal rips in the world.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.7352" lon="-64.6973"><name>Anderson Hollow Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 14] (lighthouse) Historic 1903 wooden salt-shaker pepperpot lighthouse; originally built on Salisbury Bay breakwater at Waterside, now preserved and restored at Harvey Bank Heritage Shipyard Park off Route 915.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.589" lon="-64.962"><name>Dickson Falls Lush Mossy Gorge Boardwalk</name><desc>[Day 14] (hike) Fundy National Park's most popular short hike: a 1.5 km wooden boardwalk descending into a cool, lush microclimate ravine blanketed in moss and ferns.</desc><type>hike</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.75" lon="-64.74"><name>Riverside-Albert Co-op Fuel</name><desc>[Day 14] (fuel) Route 114 Fundy coastal backup station.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.6" lon="-64.95"><name>Alma Fuel (Fundy)</name><desc>[Day 14] (fuel) Seaside village entrance to Fundy National Park.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.2596" lon="-63.6798"><name>Confederation Bridge (Outbound Toll Plaza)</name><desc>[Day 14] (ferry) Toll plaza in Borden-Carleton upon departing PEI back to New Brunswick. Motorcycle toll is ~$20.25 CAD per motorcycle.</desc><type>ferry</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.82" lon="-64.57"><name>Hopewell Rocks (Tidal Floor Walk)</name><desc>[Day 14] (sight) Walk on the ocean floor around towering flowerpot sea stack formations carved by 46-foot Fundy tides.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4108" lon="-63.3492"><name>PEI Preserve Company Restaurant (New Glasgow, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (food) 2841 New Glasgow Rd, New Glasgow, PEI. Riverside country kitchen overlooking the River Clyde — famous raspberry cream cheese pie, potato bacon soup, and artisanal preserves.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4095" lon="-63.3504"><name>New Glasgow Lobster Suppers / Lobster Pub (New Glasgow, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (food) 604 Route 258, New Glasgow, PEI. Iconic Prince Edward Island traditional lobster supper with unlimited PEI steamed mussels and homemade mile-high lemon meringue pie.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4582" lon="-63.3018"><name>Blue Mussel Café (North Rustico Harbour, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (food) 312 Harbourview Dr, North Rustico, PEI. Spectacular waterside seafood shack renowned for steamed PEI blue mussels, halibut, and seafood bake.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4892" lon="-63.3845"><name>Chez Yvonne's / Baywatch Restaurant (Cavendish, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (food) Route 6, Cavendish, PEI. Classic Cavendish family dining serving Maritime seafood platters, chowder, and lobster rolls.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4712" lon="-63.3685"><name>La Rose Bistro (Cavendish / New Glasgow, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (food) Intimate PEI bistro near Cavendish serving seasonal island produce, fresh catch, and espresso.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4915" lon="-63.3812"><name>Cavendish Fish and Chips (Cavendish, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (food) Freshly battered Atlantic haddock, PEI Russet hand-cut fries, and fried clams in the heart of Cavendish.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4904" lon="-63.3862"><name>Dave's Lobster (Cavendish Boardwalk / Charlottetown)</name><desc>[Day 14] (food) Famous PEI lobster roll shack serving warm buttered and chilled mayo lobster rolls on griddled brioche buns.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4908" lon="-63.3885"><name>Razzy's Roadhouse / Beach House (Cavendish, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (food) 8885 Cavendish Rd, Cavendish, PEI. Casual roadhouse grill serving burgers, ribs, lobster rolls, and cold draft beer.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4898" lon="-63.3935"><name>The Lost Anchor (Cavendish, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (food) 9099 Cavendish Rd, Cavendish, PEI. Maritime pub &amp; seafood eatery minutes from Cavendish Campground.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4912" lon="-63.3828"><name>The Ship's Company Pub &amp; Galley (Cavendish, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (food) Nautical-themed Cavendish pub &amp; galley serving PEI mussels, seafood chowder, and fish &amp; chips.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.2339" lon="-63.1275"><name>Sims Corner Steakhouse &amp; Oyster Bar (Charlottetown, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (food) 86 Queen St, Charlottetown, PEI. Premier PEI steakhouse and raw oyster bar featuring aged Maritime beef and freshly shucked Malpeque &amp; Raspberry Point oysters.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.2335" lon="-63.1288"><name>Claddagh Oyster House (Charlottetown, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (food) 131 Sydney St, Charlottetown, PEI. Award-winning seafood &amp; oyster house in historic Old Charlottetown.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4895" lon="-63.3818"><name>Tim Hortons (Cavendish, PEI — Route 6)</name><desc>[Day 14] (coffee) Cavendish Boardwalk / Route 6, Cavendish, PEI. Morning coffee steps from Cavendish Campground and Green Gables.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.2342" lon="-63.1268"><name>Starbucks (Charlottetown, PEI — Historic Downtown)</name><desc>[Day 14] (coffee) 154 Queen St, Charlottetown, PEI. Downtown Charlottetown coffee stop near Victoria Row and St. Dunstan's Basilica.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.2332" lon="-63.1258"><name>St. Dunstan's Basilica (Charlottetown, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (attraction) Magnificent French Gothic twin-spired stone basilica and National Historic Site in downtown Charlottetown.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4985" lon="-63.3912"><name>Cavendish Cliffs (PEI National Park)</name><desc>[Day 14] (sight) Striking rust-red sandstone sea cliffs sculpted by the Gulf of St. Lawrence waves along the Cavendish coast.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.2345" lon="-63.1272"><name>Victoria Row (Charlottetown, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (attraction) Pedestrian-only cobblestone Victorian street lined with red-brick cafés, patios, boutiques, and live music next to Confederation Centre.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4315" lon="-63.2085"><name>Brackley Beach (PEI National Park)</name><desc>[Day 14] (park) Kilometers of sweeping golden sand dunes and warm Gulf shore waters along the PEI Central Coastal Drive.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.5192" lon="-63.5512"><name>Anne of Green Gables Museum (Park Corner / Silver Bush)</name><desc>[Day 14] (attraction) Historic 1872 Campbell homestead at Park Corner overlooking the 'Lake of Shining Waters' where L.M. Montgomery was married.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4898" lon="-63.3835"><name>Avonlea Village (Cavendish, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (attraction) Turn-of-the-century heritage village in Cavendish featuring historic schoolhouse, church, and local PEI artisan food stalls.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4012" lon="-64.1285"><name>The Bottle Houses (Cap-Egmont, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (attraction) Whimsical folk-art village of three shimmering buildings and gardens constructed from over 25,000 recycled glass bottles.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4625" lon="-63.3145"><name>Prince Edward Island National Park</name><desc>[Day 14] (park) Coastal national park stretching along PEI's North Shore with red cliffs, shifting parabolic dunes, and scenic Gulf Shore Parkway.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.7058" lon="-64.2285"><name>Canadian Potato Museum (O'Leary, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (attraction) Home of the world's largest potato sculpture, heritage farm machinery hall, and PEI Potato Country Kitchen.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.5295" lon="-63.6482"><name>Thunder Cove Beach &amp; Teacup Rock (Darnley, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (sight) Spectacular hidden PEI beach featuring towering crimson sandstone caves, sea stacks, and the famous Teacup Rock formation.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.6192" lon="-64.3828"><name>West Point Lighthouse (West Point, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (lighthouse) Tallest lighthouse on Prince Edward Island (1875), striped in bold black-and-white bands overlooking the Northumberland Strait.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4312" lon="-63.8615"><name>Acadian Museum of PEI (Miscouche, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (attraction) Chronicles over 300 years of Island Acadian history and culture in Miscouche near Summerside.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.2385" lon="-63.1212"><name>Prince Edward Island Regiment Museum (Charlottetown, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (attraction) Military museum housed at Queen Charlotte Armoury showcasing PEI's regimental history from 1875 to present.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.4518" lon="-64.0725"><name>Village musical acadien (Abram-Village, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 14] (attraction) Lively Acadian cultural and musical centre in the Évangéline region featuring fiddle music, step-dancing, bakery, and crêperie.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.435" lon="-68.39"><name>de la République Provincial Park (Edmundston)</name><desc>[Day 15] (hotel-primary) Pristine provincial park 1.5 km off TCH-2 on the Madawaska River. Heated pool, hot showers, flush toilets, shaded wooded sites.</desc><type>hotel-primary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.3765" lon="-68.3251"><name>Four Points by Sheraton Edmundston</name><desc>[Day 15] (hotel-secondary) Modern hotel fallback off TCH-2 with large lighted parking and dining.</desc><type>hotel-secondary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.435" lon="-68.39"><name>Parc provincial de la République (Madawaska River)</name><desc>[Day 15] (park) Pristine New Brunswick provincial park with botanical gardens and heated pool.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.323" lon="-65.538"><name>Quaco Head Lighthouse</name><desc>[Day 15] (lighthouse) Perched on towering headland near St. Martins sea caves along the Fundy Trail Parkway; sweeping vistas of the Bay of Fundy.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2733" lon="-66.0633"><name>Saint John City Market (1876)</name><desc>[Day 15] (attraction) Canada's oldest continuously operating farmer's market, featuring a unique timber roof hand-crafted by 19th-century shipbuilders shaped like an inverted ship's hull.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.297" lon="-67.528"><name>Hartland World's Longest Covered Bridge (1901)</name><desc>[Day 15] (attraction) The longest covered wooden bridge in the world (391 m), built in 1901 across the Saint John River. You can ride your bikes right through!</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2458" lon="-66.1158"><name>Saint John Irving (Route 1 / Fairville Blvd)</name><desc>[Day 15] (fuel) Major Irving station on Route 1 / Saint John Throughway before Route 7 North with 91 Premium.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.89" lon="-66.57"><name>Fredericton Irving Big Stop</name><desc>[Day 15] (fuel) Trans-Canada Hwy 2 / Lincoln major fuel plaza with 91 Premium.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.145" lon="-67.585"><name>Woodstock Irving Big Stop</name><desc>[Day 15] (fuel) Trans-Canada Hwy 2 Saint John River valley hub with 91 Premium.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.3736" lon="-68.3253"><name>Edmundston Irving Big Stop</name><desc>[Day 15] (fuel) Last major NB fuel station before entering Quebec on Autoroute 85.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.41" lon="-65.45"><name>Fundy Trail Parkway</name><desc>[Day 15] (sight) Spectacular 30 km coastal motorcycling parkway ridden continuous from East Gate to West Gate past Walton Glen Gorge, Long Beach, Big Salmon River, and Fuller Falls to Saint John.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2597" lon="-66.0886"><name>Reversing Falls Rapids (Saint John)</name><desc>[Day 15] (sight) Spectacular tidal phenomenon where 28-foot Bay of Fundy tides force the mighty Saint John River to reverse its flow through a narrow rocky gorge.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.1152" lon="-64.8325"><name>Skipper Jack's Maritime Restaurant (Moncton, NB)</name><desc>[Day 15] (food) 211 Mapleton Rd, Moncton, NB. Lively boat-themed Maritime seafood restaurant famous for lobster rolls, fried clams, and Atlantic haddock.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.0882" lon="-64.7745"><name>Pump House Brewpub &amp; Restaurant (Moncton, NB)</name><desc>[Day 15] (food) 5 Orange Ln, Moncton, NB. Iconic Canadian craft brewery (home of Blueberry Ale) with wood-fired pizzas and pub fare.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.6012" lon="-64.9482"><name>Octopus' Garden Café &amp; Bakery (Alma / Fundy NP, NB)</name><desc>[Day 15] (food) 8598 Main St, Alma, NB. Beloved coastal café right outside Fundy National Park — famous sticky buns, espresso, paninis, and craft beer garden.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.2545" lon="-63.6942"><name>Tim Hortons (Borden-Carleton — Confederation Bridge Gateway)</name><desc>[Day 15] (coffee) 24419 Trans-Canada Hwy, Borden-Carleton, PEI. Right at the base of the 12.9 km Confederation Bridge.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.1145" lon="-64.8312"><name>Starbucks (Moncton, NB — Mapleton Rd)</name><desc>[Day 15] (coffee) 30 Wyse St / Mapleton Rd, Moncton, NB. Coffee stop en route to Hopewell Rocks and Fundy National Park.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.2125" lon="-63.4892"><name>Victoria Seaport Lighthouse (Victoria-by-the-Sea, PEI)</name><desc>[Day 15] (lighthouse) Charming 1879 square-tapered wooden range light on the wharf in the picturesque artisan village of Victoria-by-the-Sea.</desc><type>lighthouse</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.8833" lon="-72.4694"><name>Camping des Voltigeurs (Sépaq - Drummondville)</name><desc>[Day 16] (hotel-primary) Tranquil riverside Sépaq park along the Saint-François River off A-20. Clean hot showers, quiet wooded campsites, zero city congestion.</desc><type>hotel-primary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.875" lon="-72.485"><name>Hôtel Le Dauphin Drummondville</name><desc>[Day 16] (hotel-secondary) High-comfort hotel right off Highway 20 with indoor pool and restaurant.</desc><type>hotel-secondary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.8833" lon="-72.4694"><name>Camping des Voltigeurs (Sépaq Park)</name><desc>[Day 16] (park) Sépaq riverside conservation park along the Saint-François River.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.82" lon="-69.535"><name>Rivière-du-Loup Shell</name><desc>[Day 16] (fuel) Autoroute 20 / 85 junction hub with Shell V-Power 91.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.705" lon="-71.285"><name>Lévis / St-Nicolas Esso</name><desc>[Day 16] (fuel) Autoroute 20 South Shore Quebec City bypass hub with 91 Premium.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.885" lon="-72.475"><name>Drummondville Petro-Canada / A-20</name><desc>[Day 16] (fuel) Full service highway fuel plaza off A-20.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.55" lon="-68.65"><name>Dégelis Esso</name><desc>[Day 16] (fuel) Autoroute 85 Lake Témiscouata corridor backup station between Edmundston and Rivière-du-Loup.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.37" lon="-70.04"><name>La Pocatière Ultramar</name><desc>[Day 16] (fuel) Autoroute 20 South Shore backup station between Rivière-du-Loup and Lévis.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2592" lon="-66.0868"><name>The Baratie — Reversing Falls Restaurant (Saint John, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (food) 200 Bridge Rd, Saint John, NB. Rooftop &amp; dining room perched directly above the Reversing Falls rapids at Stonehammer UNESCO Global Geopark.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2718" lon="-66.0612"><name>Lemongrass Thai Fare (Saint John, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (food) 42 Princess St, Uptown Saint John, NB. Vibrant Thai restaurant and patio in the historic Trinity Royal district.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2698" lon="-66.0635"><name>Steamers Lobster Co. (Saint John, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (food) 110 Water St, Saint John, NB. Harbourside lobster boil house right on the Bay of Fundy waterfront.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2722" lon="-66.0608"><name>Britt's Pub &amp; Eatery (Saint John, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (food) 42 Princess St, Saint John, NB. Classic Uptown Saint John gastro-pub with extensive local tap list and comfort food.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2729" lon="-66.0598"><name>Picaroons General Store &amp; Brewtique (Saint John, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (food) 32 Canterbury St, Saint John, NB. New Brunswick craft beer taproom and historic general store in Uptown Saint John.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2738" lon="-66.0585"><name>Cask &amp; Kettle Irish Gastropub (Saint John, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (food) 112 Prince William St, Saint John, NB. Scratch-made Irish gastropub fare, local craft ciders, and Maritime hospitality.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2745" lon="-66.0572"><name>Splash Thai Cuisine (Saint John, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (food) Uptown Saint John favourite for fresh curries, pad thai, and quick rider lunches.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.3652" lon="-68.3278"><name>Le Café / Café Lotus Bleu (Edmundston, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (food) Downtown Edmundston artisanal café &amp; bistro serving Brayon specialties, espresso, and homemade soups.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.3688" lon="-68.3312"><name>Frank's Bar &amp; Grill (Edmundston, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (food) 135 Rue Victoria, Edmundston, NB. Landmark Edmundston steakhouse, ribs, and roadhouse grill since 1968.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.3642" lon="-68.3265"><name>Moonshin'hers Café Bistro (Edmundston, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (food) Cozy Edmundston café bistro for gourmet sandwiches, salads, and specialty coffees.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.3598" lon="-68.3295"><name>Le Deck Resto-Bar (Edmundston / Lac Baker, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (food) Lively patio resto-bar in the Edmundston region serving burgers, poutine, and local brews.</desc><type>food</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2735" lon="-66.0582"><name>Starbucks (Saint John, NB — King's Square / Uptown)</name><desc>[Day 16] (coffee) 49 King St, Saint John, NB. Uptown Saint John espresso stop near the City Market and Reversing Falls.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.0462" lon="-67.7418"><name>Tim Hortons (Grand Falls, NB — Trans-Canada Hwy 2)</name><desc>[Day 16] (coffee) 235 Madawaska Rd, Grand Falls, NB. Coffee stop overlooking the Grand Falls Gorge.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2742" lon="-66.0568"><name>Saint John Firefighters' Museum (Saint John, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (attraction) Historic No. 2 Engine House museum in Uptown Saint John displaying antique steam pumpers and Great Fire of 1877 artifacts.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2892" lon="-65.9985"><name>Little River Reservoir Park (Saint John, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (park) Tranquil lakeside urban park and walking trail network on the east side of Saint John.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2395" lon="-66.1248"><name>Saints Rest Beach (Saint John, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (sight) Sweeping Bay of Fundy sand and pebble beach adjacent to Irving Nature Park with views of Partridge Island.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2595" lon="-66.0865"><name>Reversing Falls Observation Deck (Saint John, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (sight) Dramatic lookout deck at Fallsview Park watching the monstrous Bay of Fundy tides force the Saint John River to flow backward through a narrow gorge.</desc><type>sight</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2528" lon="-66.0762"><name>Carleton Martello Tower National Historic Site (Saint John, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (attraction) 1812 circular stone coastal fortification with WWII fire-control superstructure offering 360-degree views over Saint John Harbour and the Bay of Fundy.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.2682" lon="-66.0628"><name>AREA 506 Waterfront Container Village (Saint John, NB)</name><desc>[Day 16] (attraction) Vibrant colourful shipping-container village on the Saint John waterfront featuring local vendors, murals, food trucks, and waterfront stage.</desc><type>attraction</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.7932" lon="-77.098"><name>Best Western Pembroke Inn &amp; Conference Centre</name><desc>[Day 17] (hotel-primary) Full-service motor hotel off Hwy 17 with large indoor heated pool, hot tub, fitness center, on-site restaurant, and ground-level rooms.</desc><type>hotel-primary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.185" lon="-77.685"><name>Driftwood Provincial Park (Stonecliffe / Pembroke)</name><desc>[Day 17] (hotel-secondary) Quiet provincial park along the Ottawa River with waterfront sites, hot showers.</desc><type>hotel-secondary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.185" lon="-77.685"><name>Driftwood Provincial Park (Ottawa River)</name><desc>[Day 17] (park) Quiet Ontario provincial park on Laurentian river shoreline.</desc><type>park</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.31" lon="-73.875"><name>Beauharnois Shell</name><desc>[Day 17] (fuel) Autoroute 30 bypass fuel station with 91 Premium.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.14" lon="-76.145"><name>Carleton Place Esso</name><desc>[Day 17] (fuel) Hwy 7 / Hwy 15 junction fuel station with 91 Premium.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.58" lon="-73.44"><name>Boucherville Shell</name><desc>[Day 17] (fuel) Autoroute 30 South Shore bypass strategic backup station.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.62" lon="-76.88"><name>Cobden Esso</name><desc>[Day 17] (fuel) Highway 17 Ottawa Valley corridor backup station 35 km before Pembroke.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.305" lon="-74.025"><name>Pont Serge-Marcil (A-30 Express Toll Bridge)</name><desc>[Day 17] (ferry) High-speed 2.5 km toll bridge over the St. Lawrence Seaway bypassing Montreal metro traffic on Autoroute 30.</desc><type>ferry</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.3672" lon="-68.3292"><name>Tim Hortons (Edmundston, NB)</name><desc>[Day 17] (coffee) 180 Bd Hébert, Edmundston, NB. Morning coffee before riding along Lake Temiscouata toward Rivière-du-Loup.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.8385" lon="-69.5368"><name>Starbucks (Rivière-du-Loup, QC)</name><desc>[Day 17] (coffee) 298 Bd Armand-Thériault, Rivière-du-Loup, QC. Espresso stop along the St. Lawrence south shore.</desc><type>coffee</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.656232" lon="-80.882479"><name>Hanmer Home Base (Arrival)</name><desc>[Day 18] (hotel-primary) Expedition finish line at 4671 Dupuis Drive, Hanmer, ON. Saturday afternoon completion.</desc><type>hotel-primary</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.262" lon="-78.915"><name>Eau Claire Gorges Conservation Area</name><desc>[Day 18] (hike) Dramatic 2.5 km Canadian Shield trail through an ancient granite river gorge near Mattawa with a 40-foot waterfall and 1870s logger cabin ruins.</desc><type>hike</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.315" lon="-78.705"><name>Mattawa Shell</name><desc>[Day 18] (fuel) Hwy 17 / Ottawa River corridor station with 91 Premium.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.31" lon="-79.46"><name>North Bay Shell</name><desc>[Day 18] (fuel) Hwy 17 / Hwy 11 bypass station with V-Power 91.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.205" lon="-77.495"><name>Deep River Esso</name><desc>[Day 18] (fuel) Highway 17 Ottawa River corridor backup station between Pembroke and Mattawa.</desc><type>fuel</type></wpt>
